--- !u!114 &4120551719491853241
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 3238870725464755608}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5c161357d139c154781b5f7484aabee0, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MessageGenerator
  Emails:
  - HPCshortHand: HPC
    CMSshortHand: CMS
    HPChandle: Habitable Planet Coalition
    CMShandle: Unknown Sender
    option1HPCResponseSubject: Introducing the Plasma Torus (Pro)
    option1HPCResponseContent: "To protect Planet Athanor from dangerous radiation
      and cosmic rays, we\u2019re introducing a state-of-the-art drone satellite
      swarm that can encircle a planet. It creates an orbital current of high-energy
      electrons that generate a protective artificial magnetosphere. Retrieve Boxes
      from  In Chute. Smash boxes on the floor to access parts. Once complete, place
      finished Build into Empty Out Box and place in Outgoing Chute to ship. Click
      the Build Instructions to the left of this screen for visual instructions on
      completing the Build."
    option1CMSResponseSubject: DON'T DRINK THE COFFEE
    option1CMSResponseContent: Honorable HPC Worker, My name is Professor [name redacted].
      I am contacting you on behalf of the Clockwork Multiplanetary Scientists (CMS).
      You can expect a shipment from us tomorrow. Look in the vent in your Coffee
      Room. We suspect it may become invisible if you ingest the ocular nanorobots.
    option2HPCResponseSubject: Introducing the Plasma Torus (Pro)
    option2HPCResponseContent: "Attention valuable employee. To protect Planet Athanor
      from dangerous radiation and cosmic rays, we\u2019re introducing a state-of-the-art
      drone satellite swarm that can encircle a planet. It creates an orbital current
      of high-energy electrons that generate a protective artificial magnetosphere.
      Retrieve Boxes from chute. Smash boxes on the floor to access parts. Once complete,
      place finished Build into Out Box and place in Outgoing Chute to ship."
    option2CMSResponseSubject: DON'T DRINK THE COFFEE
    option2CMSResponseContent: Honorable HPC Worker, My name is Professor [name redacted].
      I am contacting you on behalf of the Clockwork Multiplanetary Scientists (CMS).
      You can expect a shipment from us tomorrow. Look in the vent in your Coffee
      Room. We suspect it may become invisible if you ingest the ocular nanorobots.
  - HPCshortHand: HPC
    CMSshortHand: CMS
    HPChandle: Habitable Planet Coalition
    CMShandle: Clockwork Multiplanetary Scientists
    option1HPCResponseSubject: Introducing the F.I.S.C.H. Drone
    option1HPCResponseContent: "This phenomenal technology burrows into the planet\u2019s
      outer core and and swims through the molten metal, artificially creating a
      convection current that will generate the planet\u2019s natural magnetosphere.
      Proper implementation is crucial to the process. Use of non-HPC approved parts
      has been linked to critical failure of planetary interventions."
    option1CMSResponseSubject: We Discovered a Problem
    option1CMSResponseContent: "Greetings Esteemed Habitable Planet Coalition worker.
      The F.I.S.C.H. core that has been shipped to you has been made without proper
      shielding to withstand the immense pressure and temperature of the planet\u2019s
      outer core for very long. We have shipped Dense Plate Shielding to upgrade
      the Build\u2019s durability. It seems the process may have interfered with
      your camera system. We worry the HPC Coffee may obscure the appearance of our
      deliveries."
    option2HPCResponseSubject: Introducing the F.I.S.C.H. Drone
    option2HPCResponseContent: "This phenomenal technology burrows into the planet\u2019s
      outer core and and swims through the molten metal, artificially creating a
      convection current that will generate the planet\u2019s natural magnetosphere.
      Proper implementation is crucial to the process. Use of non-HPC approved parts
      has been linked to critical failure of planetary interventions."
    option2CMSResponseSubject: We Discovered a Problem
    option2CMSResponseContent: "Greetings Esteemed Habitable Planet Coalition worker.
      The F.I.S.C.H. core that has been shipped to you has been made without proper
      shielding to withstand the immense pressure and temperature of the planet\u2019s
      outer core for very long. We have shipped Dense Plate Shielding to upgrade
      the Build\u2019s durability. It seems the process may have interfered with
      your camera system. We worry the HPC Coffee may obscure the appearance of our
      deliveries."
  - HPCshortHand: HPC
    CMSshortHand: CMS
    HPChandle: Habitable Planet Coalition
    CMShandle: Clockwork Multiplanetary Scientists
    option1HPCResponseSubject: Introducing the Geodynamite
    option1HPCResponseContent: At the HPC, we believe in things going BOOM. This
      red-hot Drone Build will burrow to the Outer Core and detonate in a massive
      blast, injecting an overwhelming amount of heat energy into the convective
      current in one blast.
    option1CMSResponseSubject: Thank You For Your Help
    option1CMSResponseContent: We understand you are under contractual obligations
      with the HPC, but being honest, scientists on Athanor are terrified. Our models
      indicate that explosions large enough to heat the outer core could trigger
      a massive plume to rise to the surface, resulting in devastating volcanic activity.
      Instead, we suggest injecting the convective current with short-lived radioactive
      isotope deposits that will continually heat the core through radioactive decay
      for centuries. We plead with you to make the right choice!
    option2HPCResponseSubject: Introducing the Geodynamite
    option2HPCResponseContent: We at the HPC believe in things going BOOM. This red-hot
      Drone Build will burrow to the Outer Core and detonate in a massive blast,
      injecting an overwhelming amount of heat energy into the convective current
      in one blast. This will be your final assignment for Planet Athanor
    option2CMSResponseSubject: Please We Need Your Help
    option2CMSResponseContent: Being honest, scientists on Athanor are a tad bit
      nervous over the consequences of an explosion large enough to heat the Outer
      Core. Terrified really. Our models indicate these explosions could trigger
      a massive plume to rise to the surface, resulting in devastating volcanic activity.
      Instead, we suggest injecting the convective current with short-lived radioactive
      isotope deposits that will continually heat the core through radioactive decay
      for centuries. We plead with you to make the right choice!
  - HPCshortHand: HPC
    CMSshortHand: CMS
    HPChandle: Habitable Planet Coalition
    CMShandle: Clockwork Multiplanetary Scientists
    option1HPCResponseSubject: Introducing the Orbital Starshade
    option1HPCResponseContent: 'This precisely-machined, ultra-light technology will
      orbit Planet Melligo, intercepting light energy received from their star. This
      starshade will provide Planet Melligo with relief from its current cycle of
      excess planetary heating. '
    option1CMSResponseSubject: A Small Request
    option1CMSResponseContent: The HPC is sabotaging their own designs. Surely you
      must understand by now! An orbital starshade is far too close to the planet
      to be efficient, and its constant orbit means the starshade is only at its
      most effective position to intercept light briefly. Do they expect to charge
      us to build billions of them? I propose we retool the navigational core of
      the Build to position it at the L1 Lagrange point between Planet Melligo and
      its star. This optimal geostationary positioning will increase the amount of
      light intercepted to 1.8% of the total light energy that hits Planet Melligo,
      which will provide substantially better cooling outcomes.
    option2HPCResponseSubject: Introducing the Orbital Starshade
    option2HPCResponseContent: This precisely-machined, ultra-light technology will
      orbit Planet Melligo, intercepting light energy received from their star. This
      starshade will provide Planet Melligo with relief from its current cycle of
      excess planetary heating.
    option2CMSResponseSubject: A Small Request
    option2CMSResponseContent: Utter Ineptitude! An orbital starshade is far too
      close to the planet to be efficient, and its constant orbit means the starshade
      is only at its most effective position to intercept light briefly. Do they
      expect to charge us to build billions of them? I propose we retool the navigational
      core of the Build to position it at the L1 Lagrange point between Planet Melligo
      and its star. This optimal geostationary positioning will increase the amount
      of light intercepted to 1.8% of the total light energy that hits Planet Melligo,
      which will provide substantially better cooling outcomes.
  - HPCshortHand: HPC
    CMSshortHand: CMS
    HPChandle: Habitable Planet Coalition
    CMShandle: Clockwork Multiplanetary Scientists
    option1HPCResponseSubject: Introducing the Atmospheric Rejuvenator.
    option1HPCResponseContent: "This cutting-edge drone system is sent from stations
      on the planet\u2019s moon into the stratosphere, where it releases carbon nanoparticles.
      Conventionally called \u201Cdiamond dust,\u201D these particles scatter and
      reflect light back into space before it gets a chance to warm the planet."
    option1CMSResponseSubject: We Plead That You Will Help Us
    option1CMSResponseContent: Our research indicates that the exorbitantly expensive
      Atmospheric Rejuvenator is not attuned to the needs of our ecology. We propose
      instead injecting gaseous sulphur dioxide particles into the stratosphere,
      mimicking the cooling attained from volcanic eruptions. Our alternate core
      will contain these updated materials. This attempt to mold our intervention
      into natural processes of the planet will lead to superior outcomes.
    option2HPCResponseSubject: Introducing the Atmospheric Rejuvenator.
    option2HPCResponseContent: "This cutting-edge drone system is sent from stations
      on the planet\u2019s moon into the stratosphere, where it releases carbon nanoparticles.
      Conventionally called \u201Cdiamond dust,\u201D these particles scatter and
      reflect light back into space before it gets a chance to warm the planet."
    option2CMSResponseSubject: You Have Truly Become Melligo's Friend
    option2CMSResponseContent: We once again need you to intervene on our behalf.
      Our research indicates that the exorbitantly expensive Atmospheric Rejuvenator
      is not attuned to the needs of our ecology. We propose instead injecting gaseous
      sulphur dioxide particles into the stratosphere, mimicking the cooling attained
      from volcanic eruptions. Our alternate core will contain these updated materials. 
      This attempt to mold our intervention into natural processes of the planet
      will lead to superior outcomes.
  - HPCshortHand: HPC
    CMSshortHand: CMS
    HPChandle: Habitable Planet Coalition
    CMShandle: Clockwork Multiplanetary Scientists
    option1HPCResponseSubject: Introducing the Carbon Sink Sower
    option1HPCResponseContent: This one-of-a-kind carbon sequestration technology
      harnesses the power of hardwood to provide long-term carbon storage. By rapidly
      accelerating the planting and growth of these enormous trees we plan on pulling
      a record-breaking amount of carbon from the atmosphere. Once mature, these
      trees are uprooted and stored deep underground to remove their matter from
      the carbon-cycle.
    option1CMSResponseSubject: 'Corporate Fools! '
    option1CMSResponseContent: "Redwood takes centuries to mature! Instead: using
      Macroalgae (aka seaweed) we would borrow the power of the fastest growing biomass
      on the planet, mimicking the planet\u2019s own carbon storing mechanisms by
      sinking large quantities of seaweed into ocean trenches. This removes it from
      the terrestrial carbon cycle entirely. Please, swap in the Algae Pods before
      shipping. Our planet, and our very lives, are in peril."
    option2HPCResponseSubject: Introducing the Carbon Sink Sower
    option2HPCResponseContent: This one-of-a-kind carbon sequestration technology
      harnesses the power of hardwood to provide long-term carbon storage. By rapidly
      accelerating the planting and growth of these enormous trees we plan on pulling
      a record-breaking amount of carbon from the atmosphere. Once mature, these
      trees are uprooted and stored deep underground to remove their matter from
      the carbon-cycle.
    option2CMSResponseSubject: It's Too Slow!
    option2CMSResponseContent: "Redwood takes centuries to mature! What is the HPC
      thinking? Instead: using Macroalgae (aka seaweed) would borrow the power of
      the fastest growing biomass on the planet, mimicking the planet\u2019s own
      carbon storing mechanisms by sinking large quantities of seaweed into ocean
      trenches. This removes it from the terrestrial carbon cycle entirely. Please,
      you\u2019re the only one who can help us. Swap in the Algae Pods before shipping.
      Our planet, and our very lives, are in peril."
  - HPCshortHand: HPC
    CMSshortHand: CMS
    HPChandle: Habitable Planet Coalition
    CMShandle: Clockwork Multiplanetary Scientists
    option1HPCResponseSubject: 'Introducing the Tectonic M.O.L.E. '
    option1HPCResponseContent: "This on-the-edge-of-believable experimental technology
      burrows down to the subduction zones where the planet\u2019s tectonic plates
      push against each other, causing seismic disturbances. These drones vibrate
      in exact opposition to the seismic waves to counteract the devastating megaquakes."
    option1CMSResponseSubject: Planet Crasis Needs Your Help
    option1CMSResponseContent: "We\u2019re uncertain on the feasibility of the M.O.L.E.
      Drone. Though theoretically viable, cancelling out seismic waves requires a
      precision we do not trust HPC technology to maintain. Instead, we propose that
      you appropriate the M.O.L.E. build to CLAMP the subduction zones together.
      Our updated Grip Amplifiers and Plate Hooks will convert the Build. This drone
      series will populate the subduction zone between tectonic plates, and serve
      as a clamp binding them together. When executed correctly, our models indicate
      that this intervention will solve the megaquakes at their source."
    option2HPCResponseSubject: 'Introducing the Tectonic M.O.L.E. '
    option2HPCResponseContent: "This on-the-edge-of-believable experimental technology
      burrows down to the subduction zones where the planet\u2019s tectonic plates
      push against each other, causing seismic disturbances. These drones vibrate
      in exact opposition to the seismic waves to counteract the devastating megaquakes."
    option2CMSResponseSubject: Planet Crasis Needs Your Help
    option2CMSResponseContent: "We\u2019re uncertain on the feasibility of the M.O.L.E.
      Drone. Though theoretically viable, cancelling out seismic waves requires a
      precision we do not trust HPC technology to maintain. Instead, we propose that
      you appropriate the M.O.L.E. build to CLAMP the subduction zones together.
      Our updated Grip Amplifiers and Plate Hooks will convert the Build. This drone
      series will populate the subduction zone between tectonic plates, and serve
      as a clamp binding them together. When executed correctly, our models indicate
      that this intervention will solve the megaquakes at their source."
  - HPCshortHand: HPC
    CMSshortHand: CMS
    HPChandle: Habitable Planet Coalition
    CMShandle: Clockwork Multiplanetary Scientists
    option1HPCResponseSubject: Introducing the Stratospheric Cleanser!
    option1HPCResponseContent: This high-flying, sky-bluing, revolutionary technology
      soars through the stratosphere. Once activated, this innovative drone will
      capture the volcanic blanket of Sulfur Dioxide in our patented Sulfur Containment
      Units. This will ease the acid rains and reverse the excess cooling of Planet
      Crasis.
    option1CMSResponseSubject: Please, Double-Check the Validity of Your Science
    option1CMSResponseContent: "You can\u2019t capture enough gas from the stratosphere
      to clean the sky. It\u2019s absolutely unscientific! We\u2019d like you to
      insert this calcite particle filter Air Pump into the intake. While the air
      passes through, the calcite particles will interact chemically with the sulfur
      dioxide to nullify its harmful effects by binding together to create harmless
      gypsum particles. Please, we beg of you. Our infrastructure is too fragile
      to weather these acid rains. "
    option2HPCResponseSubject: Introducing the Stratospheric Cleanser!
    option2HPCResponseContent: This high-flying, sky-bluing, revolutionary technology
      soars through the stratosphere. Once activated, this innovative drone will
      capture the volcanic blanket of Sulfur Dioxide in our patented Sulfur Containment
      Units. This will ease the acid rains and reverse the excess cooling of Planet
      Crasis.
    option2CMSResponseSubject: Scoundrels! The HPC Is Criminally Incompetant!
    option2CMSResponseContent: "You can\u2019t capture enough gas from the stratosphere
      to clean the sky. It\u2019s absolutely unscientific! We\u2019d like you to
      insert this calcite particle filter Air Pump into the intake. While the air
      passes through, the calcite particles will interact chemically with the sulfur
      dioxide to nullify its harmful effects by binding together to create harmless
      gypsum particles.. Please, we beg of you. Our infrastructure is too fragile
      to weather these acid rains. If you do not work with us we will find a way
      to force your hand."
  - HPCshortHand: HPC
    CMSshortHand: CMS
    HPChandle: Habitable Planet Coalition
    CMShandle: Clockwork Multiplanetary Scientists
    option1HPCResponseSubject: Introducing the NORM (Naturally Occurring Radioactive
      Material) Collector
    option1HPCResponseContent: This new Build will scrub radioactive materials from
      the planetary mantle in an attempt to slow convection. When executed correctly,
      this process will cool the mantle enough to bring the convection down to a
      reasonable level and stabilize plate tectonics. We believe this will be a long-term,
      strategic solution to both the megaquake and volcanism problems of Planet Crasis.
      This will be your final assignment.
    option1CMSResponseSubject: We're Desperate
    option1CMSResponseContent: "Can you not see that the HPC is sending this planet
      to its doom? The effect of radioactive decay on Mantle Convection is negligible
      in comparison to the amount of heat transferred from the outer core. We ask
      you to swap in our LLVP Builder. Our alternate drone would instead build a
      BLANKET between the mantle and outer core, slowing down the out-of-control
      convection by creating large masses of dense material that will stand in the
      way of more rapid convection. Please build this final drone for us. It\u2019s
      our only hope."
    option2HPCResponseSubject: Introducing the NORM (Naturally Occurring Radioactive
      Material) Collector
    option2HPCResponseContent: This new Build will scrub radioactive materials from
      the planetary mantle in an attempt to slow convection. When executed correctly,
      this process will cool the mantle enough to bring the convection down to a
      reasonable level and stabilize plate tectonics. We believe this will be a long-term,
      strategic solution to both the megaquake and volcanism problems of Planet Crasis.
      This will be your final assignment.
    option2CMSResponseSubject: A Final Request
    option2CMSResponseContent: "Thank you for all the help you have given us, but
      we need your help one more time. The HPC is wrong again! The effect of radioactive
      decay on Mantle Convection is negligible in comparison to the amount of heat
      transferred from the outer core. We ask you to swap in our LLVP Builder. Our
      alternate drone would instead build a BLANKET between the mantle and outer
      core, slowing down the out-of-control convection by creating large masses of
      dense material that will stand in the way of more rapid convection. Please
      build this final drone for us. It\u2019s our only hope."
  sendEmail: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8ce999a2635ee944da23c29969c8c5f4, type: 2}
